<section class="editorial-hero bleed-full"><div class="container editorial-hero__inner"><div class="editorial-hero__copy"><p class="kicker">About Hakuba / Wroughton &amp; Mevagissey</p><h1>Meet your dojo.</h1><div class="editorial-hero__intro"><p>Karate for children aged 7+, teenagers and adults in Wroughton, Swindon and Mevagissey, Cornwall. You can start with no experience: our instructors introduce the basics and help you find your feet.</p><p>We are a non-profit club. Traditional training, a local community and a welcoming place to begin.</p></div><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/contact')); ?>" data-discover="true">Ask about a free class</a></div></div></section><section class="editorial-split"><figure class="editorial-split__image"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/optimized/cornwall-course-group-2026-1280.webp')); ?>" srcset="<?php echo esc_attr(hakuba_srcset('/images/optimized/cornwall-course-group-2026-640.webp 640w, /images/optimized/cornwall-course-group-2026-1280.webp 1280w')); ?>" sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 560px, (min-width: 700px) 46vw, 92vw" alt="Hakuba members gathered for a group photograph at the September 2026 Cornwall course" width="1280" height="960" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Cornwall course / September 2026</figcaption></figure><div class="editorial-split__copy"><p class="kicker">The people behind your practice</p><h2>Local instruction.<br>Shared standards.</h2><h3>Wroughton / Swindon</h3><p>Rob Wall Sensei (4th Dan) and Andrea Bond Sensei (3rd Dan) run Wroughton classes. Jim Rendell Sensei also attends Wroughton gradings.</p><h3>Mevagissey / Cornwall</h3><p>Jim Rendell Sensei (4th Dan) leads training in Mevagissey, with guidance from Gary Swift Sensei.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-split"><div><p class="kicker">New to karate?</p><h2>You do not need<br>to know it all.</h2><p>In class, you practise basic movements, work on sequences of techniques and learn controlled partner exercises. Respect and consideration for your training partners are part of the lesson, not something you are expected to arrive knowing.</p></div><div><h3>Children, teenagers and adults</h3><p>Children work on concentration, coordination and confidence. Teenagers and adults build fitness and self-defence foundations through steady practice. Wroughton has junior, adult and mixed sessions; Mevagissey offers a family and adult session.</p><h3>Your first visit</h3><p>Choose a suitable class and arrive a few minutes early. No booking is needed; contact us if you would like help choosing a session. Comfortable training clothes and water are enough to start: you do not need to buy a gi before trying karate.</p><a class="cta-button cta-button--secondary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/beginners')); ?>" data-discover="true">See what your first class involves</a></div></section><?php hakuba_class_link(); ?><section class="editorial-band bleed-full"><div class="container editorial-band__inner"><div><p class="kicker">Wado-Ryu</p><h2>Tradition with<br>a purpose.</h2></div><div><p>Hakuba follows the teachings of Grandmaster Hironori Otsuka and the traditional Japanese approach of Rei, Kihon, Kumite and Kata. These are not four separate destinations: they support each other throughout your training.</p><p>As a beginner, you do not need to know the Japanese terms or arrive with a particular level of fitness. Your instructor introduces the fundamentals and helps you build from there.</p></div></div></section><section><p class="kicker">On the dojo floor</p><h2>Four foundations. One practice.</h2><div class="foundation-grid"><article><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/rei2.jpg')); ?>" alt="Rei: respect in karate training" loading="lazy"><h3>Rei <small>Respect</small></h3><p>Respect and dojo etiquette create a positive environment for everyone on the floor.</p></article><article><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/video-stills/1121619617203683-7s.jpg')); ?>" alt="Kihon: the fundamentals in karate training" loading="lazy"><h3>Kihon <small>The fundamentals</small></h3><p>Practise the basics carefully. Reliable movement starts with a strong foundation.</p></article><article><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/video-stills/partner-practice-detail.jpg')); ?>" alt="Kumite: working together in karate training" loading="lazy"><h3>Kumite <small>Working together</small></h3><p>Controlled partner work develops timing, distance and an understanding of technique.</p></article><article><div class="foundation-type" aria-hidden="true"><span>Practice / Precision</span><strong>Kata</strong></div><h3>Kata <small>Purposeful movement</small></h3><p>Sequences of techniques connect the fundamentals and give students a way to deepen their practice.</p></article></div></section><section class="editorial-split editorial-split--reverse"><figure class="editorial-split__image instructor-photo"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/sensei-james-rendell.jpg')); ?>" alt="Jim Rendell Sensei, 4th Dan" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="kicker">Part of the wider Wado community</p><h2>Connected by tradition.</h2><p>Hakuba Karate is a member of the British Wado Federation and International Wado Federation.</p><ul class="resource-index federation-index"><li><a href="https://britishwadofederation.org.uk/"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('bwf-logo.jpg')); ?>" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">British Wado Federation<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li><li><a href="https://iwf-karate.org/"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('iwf-logo.png')); ?>" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">International Wado Federation<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li></ul><p>Our aim is steady, safe progression: respect for the art, consideration for your training partners and a clear path from your first lesson onwards.</p></div></section><section class="join-band bleed-full"><div class="container join-band__inner"><div><p class="kicker">Wroughton / Mevagissey</p><h2>Come and meet your dojo.</h2><p>Beginners welcome, from age 7. Choose a suitable class and arrive a few minutes early. No booking needed. Contact us if you would like help choosing.</p></div><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/classes/#class-times')); ?>" data-discover="true">View class times <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></div></section>
